                <pb facs="0696" n="616" xml:id="pg616"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Powell.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-07-26"><hi rendition="#italic">July 26,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Adee acknowledges the receipt of Mr. Powell’s two telegrams, and says that
                    the rule as to piracy is stated in instruction of December 15, 1883, to Mr.
                    Langston, Mr. Powell’s predecessor.)</p>
            </div>
